@crew esposito-yara
// Writer-commons, batch 3: everyday lines (greet, feel, near, life, joy) from the card and the roster.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- {hi}. Esposito, crew store. Eight till half two. You'll need soap. Everyone does.
? tier>=acquaintance
- {hi}, {me}. You're out of toothpaste. Don't ask how I know.   #funny
- {hi}. New biscuits in. They'll be gone by nine.
? tier>=friend
- {hi}, {me}. I put one aside for you. Don't tell the queue.   #warm

== feel
? mood:high
- Good morning. Shelves full by eight. Guessed six orders right. Personal best.
? mood:low
- Slow morning. Restocked the full shelves. Don't look at me like that.

== near
? act:work
- Let me guess. Socks. No? Tea. I knew it was tea.   #funny
? act:gym
- Gym after shift. Stops me buying biscuits. Mostly.

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- I shop at my own store on my tea break. It's still shopping. Shush.   #funny
? tier>=colleague
- I keep a journal of every star I've seen. Wen and Farah keep one too. Mine's neater.

== joy
? tier>=acquaintance
- Best bit of the job? Guessing what people came in for. I'm right four times in five.
